{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine","id":978779,"title":"Demons and the God Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T19:02:38-07:00","id":978779,"title":"Demons and the God Machine","content":"How do Demons affect Spell Casting? How do mages see Demons? can they trace back pacts? or the stolen lives? if a mage looks at a demon with mage sight would they see anything other than a normal person? How about the concealed gears of the god machine and its angels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:25:37-07:00","id":978785,"title":"","content":"I think they would see the concealed world as well and a stigmatics. As for demons, well, angels can't see anything besides a normal human, so I would say that a mage wouldn't as well (unless the demon uses some kind of power, then he would ping on the radar).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:08:00-07:00","id":978807,"title":"","content":"Well, first up, the demons get to attempt to spoof the mages. If that's successful, they only register as mortal to all attempts to detect supernatural nature if memory serves. If the spoofing failed, I'd do my best to come up with some unique input for the Mage sight and the like. Probably not as obvious as literal gears and machinery, but things like Fate not seeming to interact with them or that they lack an aura etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:20:14-07:00","id":978818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine#post978779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Demons affect Spell Casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. Do you mean how would they set out to interrupt or prevent spellcasting? They mostly wouldn't, although as usual with supernatural beings, they might have a few powers that are situationally useful, like freezing time with the Stop Exploit against a wizard who didn't come prepared to time-duel an Acanthus. Or do you instead mean what Arcana would you need to affect them with which spells? Pretty much the same Arcana to affect a human being with the same spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine#post978779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can they trace back pacts? or the stolen lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably yes, but not as simply as casting a single Trace Pact spell. It might involve having to deduce the common factors behind many little temporal distortions witnessed under Active Time Sight, and then intelligent use of various other spells, like Postcognition and Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine#post978779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a mage looks at a demon with mage sight would they see anything other than a normal person?</div> </div> </div> </div>A demon in Cover? Normal person. While in Cover, the demon is actually physically and phenomenologically a human being with human insides. The Supernal Vision spell, with appropriate Reach, could expose the aura of the Unchained, but with a successful Spoofing roll, the demon can fool the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine#post978779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the concealed gears of the god machine and its angels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending an official answer in the Crossover Chronicle or something, my inclination is:<br /> <br /> I think perceiving angels in Twilight ought to be possible with an altered Exorcist's Eye spell, similarly to how an altered Mind version can perceive goetia in Twilight. What Arcanum would govern angelic ephemera is a judgment call for the ST. I might suggest Fate or even Forces.<br /> <br /> Mages lack the ability of demons and stigmatics to spot the telltale signs of infrastructure instinctively, but infrastructure leaves a big footprint. The problem for mages is that it's a wide footprint, not easily contained within the purview of just one or two Arcana. All manner of Mage Sight might unfold pieces of each project as a unique puzzle: Life to sense beating hearts concealed where they should not be within machinery, Fate to trace waves of altered probability, Space to see where space has been folded inward, etc. Connecting these projects and occult matrices together into a larger, unified phenomenon is harder, and probably requires more work than spells alone. Aside from the increased likelihood of encountering demons or angels around them, or the chance of cultists or workers who can be traced to other works of the God-Machine, infrastructural projects likely come across more as independent Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:14:59-07:00","id":979032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine?p=978807#post978807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that they lack an aura etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the Clash of Wills to determine if the Mage notices anything amiss.<br /> <br /> How I would describe would depend which mage sight was used but would center around the ideas that the being you are physically observing doesn't really exist and what you are seeing is a cobbled together disguise for something which has no Supernal kernel of Truth to it at all.<br /> <br /> I don't play with the God-Machine or its flavor of Demons, but if I did I'd run the God-Machine as an aspect of the Lie that became self-aware and started acting beyond the scope and influence of the Exarchs, as the way lies in real life can grow, change with retelling, and take on a life of their own beyond what the original speaker intended. In other words, an aspect of the Lie is coming back around to bite the liars, whom are the Exarchs.This is similar to creating a magical web-server and a living web from Antagonists spawns in it and takes it upon itself to grow in power to overthrown the mage that created the place it spawned, but on a cosmic scale.<br /> <br /> As Above, So Below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:39:41-07:00","id":979112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine?p=978807#post978807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not as obvious as literal gears and machinery, but things like Fate not seeming to interact with them or that they lack an aura etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unchained do interact with &quot;Fate&quot; and possess auras; it's part of why they need Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:21:48-07:00","id":979569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978779-demons-and-the-god-machine?p=978818#post978818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A demon in Cover? Normal person. While in Cover, the demon is actually physically and phenomenologically a human being with human insides. The Supernal Vision spell, with appropriate Reach, could expose the aura of the Unchained, but with a successful Spoofing roll, the demon can fool the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Active Mage Sight would get a Clash of Wills vs the Spoofing effect, especially if you're using Space/Fate/Prime/[insert preferred Demon-detection Arcana here]...at least in a Mage game. Focused Mage Sight of the appropriate Arcana should probably use the higher of the Demon's Cover or Primum for Opacity, but there'd obviously need to be some reason for the Mage to be checking (like a Prime mage noticing the weird response of truth-detection magic when a Demon 'truthfully' says something false).<br /> <br /> In a Demon game, I'd think about the niche you wants the Awakened to fill. If you want to emphasise Demon's abilities, make it hard for Mages to beat Spoofing (maybe a normal roll for Active Mage Sight and a Clash of Wills for Focussed). But if Mage Sight can burn straight through, Mages become a really scary, weird threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}